part voice_coil "Voice-coil actuator"
category Actuators
summary "A coil in a permanent-magnet gap: force proportional to current in both directions, over its whole stroke."
explain "A current i in a coil of wire length l in field B feels F = B·l·i; moving at speed v it generates a back-EMF B·l·v. With k = B·l (force constant) it is the linear twin of a DC motor: L·di/dt = V − R·i − k·v. The force acts between coil and magnet."
tradeoffs "Smooth, fast, cog-free, bidirectional force with no backlash: ideal for haptics, fast focus and force-controlled grippers. But force per watt is low and stroke is short (millimetres to centimetres); a motor with a screw or belt goes further and holds loads more efficiently."
limits "Constant force constant over the stroke (real ones fall off near the ends), no end stops, constant resistance."
pairs translational.mass translational.spring part.hard_stop_linear sensor.force electrical.controlled_voltage_source translational.ground
port p electrical
port n electrical
port coil translational
port magnet translational
param force_constant N/A ~ 5 "Force per amp, B·l (also back-EMF volts per m/s)"
param resistance Ω ~ 4 "Coil resistance"
param inductance H = 0.001 "Coil inductance"
realtime inductance = 0
state i Current = 0
let v = coil.v - magnet.v
eq inductance*der(i) = p.v - n.v - resistance*i - force_constant*v
flow p = i
flow n = -i
flow coil = -force_constant*i
flow magnet = force_constant*i
energy 0.5*inductance*i^2
derive "stall force per volt" = force_constant/resistance N/V
derive "motor constant squared (force² per watt)" = force_constant^2/resistance N^2/W
